[{"id":"z-fill","itemId":"high-impedance","role":"core","promptHtml":"While <code class=\"nobreak\">oe</code> is 0, <code class=\"nobreak\">pin</code> must be let go: nothing may drive it. Type the value that does that.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">1'bz</code> is one bit of Z, not driven. While <code class=\"nobreak\">oe</code> is 0 the conditional gives it, so the module lets go of <code class=\"nobreak\">pin</code>; Vivado builds this as an OBUFT at the pin (lesson 3.2). <code class=\"nobreak\">1'b0</code> would drive the pin low, which is not the same as letting go.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-03/pin_hold/pin_hold.sv","firstLine":1,"totalLines":18,"before":["// Holds one bit and puts it on a pin only while oe (output enable) is 1.","// q has no reset, so the code never says what it starts at.","// While oe is 0, the module lets go of the pin: nothing drives it.","module pin_hold (","  input  logic clk,","  input  logic load,   // at a rising edge, q takes d when load is 1","  input  logic d,","  input  logic oe,     // output enable","  output logic pin",");","  logic q;","","  always_ff @(posedge clk) begin","    if (load) q <= d;","  end",""],"blankLine":{"left":"  assign pin = oe ? q : ","right":";"},"after":["endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"// Holds one bit and puts it on a pin only while oe (output enable) is 1.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// q has no reset, so the code never says what it starts at.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// While oe is 0, the module lets go of the pin: nothing drives it.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"pin_hold","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" load,   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// at a rising edge, q takes d when load is 1","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" oe,     ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// output enable","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" pin","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (load) q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" pin ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" oe ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"?","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]},"after":[[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["1'bz","1'hz","1'oz","1'dz","'z"],"caseSensitive":false,"blankLabel":"The missing value"},{"id":"z-predict-floating","itemId":"high-impedance","role":"core","promptHtml":"Z is drawn on the half-way line. In this copy of lesson 0.2's alarm, nothing drives <code class=\"nobreak\">window_open</code>: the testbench connects it to <code class=\"nobreak\">1'bz</code>. <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is <code>armed &amp; opening</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is <code>door_open | window_open</code>. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> for each step: 0, 1 or X.","explanationHtml":"<p>Logic that reads a Z works it out as if it were X (lesson 3.2). With the door open, <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is 1 | Z, which is 1, so <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">armed</code>: 1 in steps 0 and 5, and 0 in step 3. With the door closed, <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is X, so <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is X where <code class=\"nobreak\">armed</code> is 1 (steps 1, 4 and 7) and 0 where it is 0 (steps 2 and 6). <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is never Z: <code class=\"nobreak\">&amp;</code> always gives 0, 1 or X.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"alarm-z-window","source":"hdl/level-03/alarm_x/alarm_x_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"armed","path":"alarm_x_tb.armed2","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[2,"0"],[4,"1"],[6,"0"],[7,"1"]]},{"label":"door_open","path":"alarm_x_tb.door2","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[3,"1"],[4,"0"],[5,"1"],[6,"0"]]},{"label":"window_open","path":"alarm_x_tb.dut2.window_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"z"]]},{"label":"siren","path":"alarm_x_tb.siren2","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"x"],[2,"0"],[4,"x"],[5,"1"],[6,"0"],[7,"x"]],"samples":["1","x","0","0","x","1","0","x"],"allowX":true}]},"answer":"siren"},{"id":"z-find-bug","itemId":"high-impedance","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">pin</code> should show <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> while <code class=\"nobreak\">oe</code> is 1, and be let go while <code class=\"nobreak\">oe</code> is 0. The testbench's first failure is <code>pin=x, expected z at 6 ns</code>, while <code class=\"nobreak\">oe</code> is still 0. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p>In <code>oe ? 1'bz : q</code>, the value after <code class=\"nobreak\">?</code> is for <code class=\"nobreak\">oe</code> at 1 and the one after <code class=\"nobreak\">:</code> is for <code class=\"nobreak\">oe</code> at 0 (lesson 1.3). So this line lets go of <code class=\"nobreak\">pin</code> while <code class=\"nobreak\">oe</code> is 1, and drives it with <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> while <code class=\"nobreak\">oe</code> is 0: at 6 ns <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> has never been loaded, so <code class=\"nobreak\">pin</code> shows X where it should be Z (lesson 3.2). Written <code>oe ? q : 1'bz</code>, it does what the comment says. The <code class=\"nobreak\">always_ff</code> block is right as it is.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-03/pin_hold_bug/pin_hold_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// Holds one bit and puts it on a pin only while oe (output enable) is 1.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// q has no reset, so the code never says what it starts at.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// While oe is 0, the module lets go of the pin: nothing drives it.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"pin_hold_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" load,   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// at a rising edge, q takes d when load is 1","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" oe,     ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// output enable","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" pin","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (load) q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" pin ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" oe ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"?","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1'bz","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" q;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":17,"fixLine":"assign pin = oe ? q : 1'bz;"},{"id":"z-report-obuft","itemId":"high-impedance","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built lesson 3.2's <code class=\"nobreak\">pin_hold.sv</code> for the Arty A7-100T, with <code class=\"nobreak\">pin</code> on LED LD4. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses. An OBUFT is an output buffer that can stop driving its pin.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the OBUFT row. <code class=\"nobreak\">pin</code> is the only port that ever lets go, and inside an FPGA only a pin can, so Vivado puts one tri-state buffer at that pin (lesson 3.2). The IBUF row counts the input pins, the FDRE holds <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code>, the BUFG carries the clock, and the LUT1 turns <code class=\"nobreak\">oe</code> into the buffer's &quot;stop driving&quot; input.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/pin_hold/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":179,"excerpt":["8. Primitives","-------------","","+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| IBUF     |    4 |                  IO |","| OBUFT    |    1 |                  IO |","| LUT1     |    1 |                 LUT |","| FDRE     |    1 |        Flop & Latch |","| BUFG     |    1 |               Clock |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many OBUFT cells did Vivado use?","answer":"1","numeric":true}]